	(text "The ring's VIH is 0.7*VLED. On the cell that peaked at 2.94V and the MCU drove pixel 1" (at 429.98 411.42 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "39949657-6a6c-5295-9cea-d633f28918c2"))
	(text "directly; on VSYS it is 3.29V (3.5V at a 5.25V port), past anything a 3.3V pad can" (at 429.98 414.08 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "4d991db4-b1c5-57e4-b5eb-a2583aab185f"))
	(text "output. Q3 inverts into R23's pull-up, so the swing is a full VLED rail whatever VLED is" (at 429.98 416.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "b3679aa3-5658-5604-8937-58d827d2dca3"))
	(text "— 3.0V cell or 5.0V cable. Only pixel 1 needs it; every DI after that is driven by the" (at 429.98 419.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "6c23b6be-df5d-557c-a8ce-18c554571c43"))
	(text "previous DO. Firmware must set gpio_set_outover(LED_DATA, GPIO_OVERRIDE_INVERT) — the pad" (at 429.98 422.06 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "439a648f-f0dd-54a2-8b17-8aff9bf73a2d"))
	(text "override sits after the PIO, so the NeoPixel program is untouched." (at 429.98 424.72 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "142ea7e9-95f4-5cae-8be5-4cd29f0f9761"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 424.98 351.02) (xy 524.692 351.02) (xy 524.692 429.72) (xy 424.98 429.72) (xy 424.98 351.02))
